    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 15th with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who commands our highest daily efficiency score at 82.13. His matchup against Lorenzen is optimal, buoyed by a significant +14% platoon edge and the leadoff spot in the order, making him our primary target for stolen bases\u2014a category we are aggressively hunting. Following closely is **Junior Caminero** (73.41), whose +15% SP skill adjustment against Lauer highlights a rare day where we can capitalize on a favorable matchup against a veteran lefty. While **Trea Turner** (62.70) faces a tougher test against Gusto, his elite speed and the increased likelihood of green lights against a slower delivery profile keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier, essential for maintaining our lead in the speed categories.\n\nOur lineup construction favors aggressive upside despite some challenging matchups for the middle of our order. **Yordan Alvarez** (58.67) and **Kyle Schwarber** (59.73) remain mandatory starts even with sub-optimal SP matchups, as their raw power and xwOBA profiles create a high floor that outweighs the risk of the individual SP assignments. The most difficult bench decision involved the proximity of **Colt Keith** (55.73) to our starting threshold; while he earns his spot today against Teng due to a favorable +7% platoon edge, he narrowly edged out the production we might expect from the rest of the bench. Unfortunately, our depth is constrained by the absences of **Christian Yelich** and **Caleb Durbin** due to team off-days, while **Hyeseong Kim** and **Rece Hinds** remain sidelined in the minors, limiting our ability to rotate for higher efficiency.\n\nWe must monitor the weather and official lineups closely, particularly for **Carson Benge** (45.45) and **Dillon Dingler** (41.34). While **Carson Benge** benefits from the leadoff spot, his score is suppressed by a -19% SP skill penalty against Burns; any lineup shifts further down the order would risk dropping him into \"Below floor\" territory. Similarly, **Dillon Dingler** remains our most marginal start today; his dynamic platoon disadvantage against the right-handed Teng is a concern, and he is the first candidate to be pulled if we need to preserve game caps to protect our seasonal lead. We will proceed with this configuration, banking on the stolen base upside of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Trea Turner** to provide the necessary separation in a tight 5x5 race.",
